  "notes": "Vendor rows from the tech specs page read 2026-11-20: **Total PoE Availability - 200-240V AC shared mode: 2,150 W with (2) 1,200 W modules; 100-120V AC shared mode: 1,850 W; 200-240V AC redundant mode: 1,050 W; 100-120V AC redundant mode: 850 W**, **Max. PoE Output up to PoE+++**, per-port wattage by PSE **PoE 15.4 W / PoE+ 30 W / PoE++ 60 W / PoE+++ 90 W**, **2,400 W max power consumption including PoE output**, (2) hot-swappable PSUs and (4) hot-swappable fans. **The budget is a function of mains voltage and PSU mode, not one number**: the same chassis in a 100-120 V rack with redundant feed hands out 850 W, a third of the 2,150 W headline this entry quotes, so the field records the vendor's maximum (shared mode, two 1,200 W modules) and the conditions ride in this note."
